From 98891b86c8a66e0fe6705fcb6e3fe4254c2af3d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:24:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(methane): wetland-tile vegetation from its GLWD make-up
 instead of the five-zone proxy (C-13)

Ledger C-13 (paper V2), switch wetland_veg_glwd, off by default. The
five-zone climate proxy gave every tropical peat-rich wetland papyrus
aerenchyma (porosity 0.5, 8 mm, 3 gC tillers, NPP 600) although 80% of
GLWD tropical wetland is forested peat, and switched aerenchyma off above
50N once the peat carbon profile lowered topsoil organic matter.

With the switch on, a new module reads the forested share and class areas
of the tile per grid cell (v2/scripts/glwd_class_2deg.py) and, per wetland
patch: NPP is the tile's assimilation times wetland_npp_frac, split by a
forest-weighted belowground share (wetland_bg_frac_forest 0.15 for
forested wetland); roots follow the land class's profile; aerenchyma uses
the CLM4Me grass defaults with the forested share at nongrassporosratio;
and after each LAI read the non-forested share keeps its remote-sensing
LAI only up to the measured peak (open peatland 0.6, marsh 3).

